To add to the recent questions on sacrificing, I would like to know what
determines when you receive an artifact from your god. Sometimes I have
sacrificed till luck maxed out (ie: no more messages about four leaf
clovers) and not got one, but in one game as a Barbarian, I found an
altar on level 1, sacrificed a newt corpse (first sacrifice) and got
given Stormbringer! (V3.0 pl7) Since newts normally do nothing when
sacrificed, unless you are converting an altar, this would seem to
indicate that the game first determines whether you get an object, then
decides on the value of the corpse and whether luck increases.
Anyone know the answers?

